#                           elements is even; otherwise, sorted in ascending order.
#         - "went_below_zero": A boolean flag indicating whether the running partial sum ever went below zero.
#     # Description in natural language
#     This function takes a list of non-negative integers and calculates a partial sum while iterating through
#     the list. If the partial sum ever dips below zero, a flag ("went_below_zero") is set to True. Afterward,
#     based on the sum of the first and last element of the list, it sorts the entire list either in
#     descending order (if the sum mod 2 == 0) or ascending order (if the sum mod 2 != 0). It returns a dictionary
#     with both the sorted list and the flag indicating if the partial sum went below zero.
#     # Examples
#     >>> sort_array([21, 14, 23, 11])
#     {'sorted_result': [23, 21, 14, 11], 'went_below_zero': False}
#     >>> sort_array([15, 42, 87, 32 ,11, 0])
